    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38546" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Prŏdĭcus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πρόδικος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Grecian sophist of
				Ceos</i>, <i>contemporary with Socrates</i>, 
			
			<i>author of the story of The Choice of Hercules</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Brut. 8, 30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de Or. 3, 32, 128</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 3,
				1, 12</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Prŏdĭcĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Prodicus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Prodicius Hercules,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Off. 1, 32, 118</span></i>
			.</div>
